# Decisions log — Paper 2

Append-only chronological record of protocol amendments and methodological deviations.
Every entry is timestamped and justified. Reported transparently in the manuscript Methods.

---

## #001 — 2026-05-21 — Sample size expanded from 200 to ≥400 nodules
**Trigger:** Independent verification pass (general-purpose verification agent, transcript on file).
**Issue:** N=200 (100/100) yields minimum-detectable ΔAUC ≈ 0.045 under DeLong-paired α=0.05, β=0.20, ρ≈0.85, which would mask sub-clinically-meaningful effects and force descriptive-only reframing.
**Decision:** Expand to N≥400 (200/200). Loosen median-diameter floor from 10 mm to 8 mm if needed to reach target. Sensitivity analysis at ≥10 mm preserves comparability to the pre-amendment design.
**Impact on timeline:** +6-10 h for the larger feature extraction; absorbed in Week 2 slack.

## #002 — 2026-05-21 — Two parallel radiomics arms added (RAD-3D + RAD-2D)
**Trigger:** Verification-pass concern 3 (2D-vs-3D unfairness).
**Issue:** Central-axial-slice FM inference vs full-volume PyRadiomics conflates paradigm (FM vs radiomics) with dimensionality (2D vs 3D). Single-reviewer kill-shot risk.
**Decision:** Add RAD-2D arm using PyRadiomics on the same central axial slice the FM sees, with `shape2D` substituted for `shape`. RAD-3D remains as upper-bound reference; H1 / H2 primary tests now run FM vs RAD-2D for apples-to-apples comparison.
**Impact on code:** `04_extract_radiomics.py` must accept a `--mode {3d,2d}` flag and produce `radiomics_features_3d.parquet` and `radiomics_features_2d.parquet`.
**Impact on timeline:** +4 h extraction.

## #003 — 2026-05-21 — ICC(2,1) becomes primary statistic; ICC(3,1) demoted to supplementary
**Trigger:** Verification-pass concern 1.
**Issue:** ICC(3,1) assumes fixed raters / fixed conditions and does not licence generalisation beyond them. Our 4 readers are a sample and our 9 perturbations are illustrative; we want to generalise.
**Decision:** ICC(2,1) two-way random, absolute agreement, single rater, becomes the primary statistic. ICC(3,1) reported in supplementary for backward compatibility with the radiomics literature. Stability threshold remains 0.75.
**Impact on code:** `06_compute_icc.py` must extract the ICC2 row from pingouin output (currently extracts ICC3).

## #004 — 2026-05-21 — Nested 5-fold CV for downstream classifier; ICC selection fold-internal only
**Trigger:** Verification-pass concern 4 (H4 double-dipping; also threatens H2).
**Issue:** Selecting features by ICC computed on the full set, then training on overlapping CV folds, leaks information and inflates apparent stability-vs-performance correlation.
**Decision:** Inside each outer training fold, compute ICC on training data only; select features at threshold τ; fit L2 logistic regression on training portion; evaluate on held-out outer fold. Report Jaccard selection-stability across folds in supplementary.
**Impact on code:** `07_downstream_classifier.py` requires substantive rewrite (estimated 3-4 h).

## #005 — 2026-05-21 — Perturbation magnitudes capped & Dice-calibrated tier added
**Trigger:** Verification-pass concern 5.
**Issue:** 3-voxel dilation on a 10 mm nodule = ~40 % volume inflation, well outside empirical LIDC inter-reader variability (Dice 0.70-0.85; mean surface distance 1-2 voxels).
**Decision:** Remove 3-voxel dilation. Add a single Dice-calibrated synthetic mask per nodule, generated by adaptive morphological perturbation tuned to match the median pairwise reader Dice for that nodule. Total perturbations per nodule: 12 instead of 13.
**Impact on code:** `03_generate_perturbations.py` PERTURBATION_SPEC modified; new helper function `dice_calibrated_perturbation()` added.

## #006 — 2026-05-21 — Manuscript framing repositioned explicitly against Pai 2025
**Trigger:** Verification-pass novelty verdict (PARTIALLY PRE-EMPTED).
**Issue:** Pai 2025 TumorImagingBench (PMC12154149) is the most threatening prior work; reviewer 2 will cite it.
**Decision:** Introduction now leads with explicit 4-point differentiation against Pai 2025 (per-dimension ICC vs global cosine; segmentation perturbation vs scan-repeat; FM + radiomics head-to-head vs FM-only; downstream task pre-vs-post-filter vs none). Manuscript Section 4.2 (Comparison to existing literature) given a dedicated paragraph on this comparison.

