## #010 — 2026-05-21/22 — TCIA NBIA API endpoint migrated v4 → v1; LIDC download completed (199/200 patients, 9.11 GB)
**Trigger:** First run of `01_download_lidc.py` timed out at the manifest-listing step. The `services/v4/TCIA/query/...` endpoint that the original script used is deprecated as of May 2026 and returns hangs / 500s. Discovered live during Week-1 Saturday download.
**Decision:** Switched the script to the current `nbia-api/services/v1/...` endpoint. URL change in two places: `list_series()` → `/getSeries` (no `/query/`); `download_series()` → `/getImage`. Per-call timeout raised from 60 s to 300 s. v1 returns the full LIDC-IDRI manifest (15 116 series across 1 010 patients) in ~18 s.
**Verification:** `python 01_download_lidc.py --n_cases 200` completed exit 0 after 14.1 h wall-time; 199 of 200 patient cases downloaded (9.11 GB total under `data/raw/LIDC-IDRI-XXXX/`). One series failed (`LIDC-IDRI-0049` series `...775427`) — handled gracefully by the per-series try/except. ~45 MB/patient typical (CT-only filter applied).
**Known limitation of the patched script (not yet fixed):** the 300 s timeout is *per-chunk read*, not per-series overall. A wedged connection where bytes drip in slowly enough to never trip the chunk timeout can hang for hours. This caused a ~12 h stall on a single series during this run; remaining 151 series completed in ~50 minutes at normal pace afterwards. Defensive patch deferred until / unless a re-download is needed (see manuscript revision plan).
**Files updated:** `code/01_download_lidc.py` lines 33-45 (already patched in-place by user during the live debugging session).

